I would like to include function calls when throwing errors from inside a setter function. Due to the complexity of the call stack, `rlang::caller_env()` does not work (see below). What would be the best way to include the function call? Thanks! 
(Currently, my best idea is to use `rlang::trace_back()` and craft the call based on its first entry.)

```r
library(S7)
library(rlang)
library(cli)

testclass <- new_class("testclass",
  properties = list(
    pro = new_property(
      class = class_character,
      validator = function(value) {
        if (identical(value, "hello")) {
          "must not be hello"
        }
      },
      setter = function(self, value) {
        if (identical(value, "hello")) {
          cli_abort("Can't do that.",
                    call = caller_env())
        }

        self@pro <- value
        self
      }
    )
  )
)

t <- testclass(pro = "hello")
#> Error:
#> ! Can't do that.
```

